I am validating a variant-calling pipeline where an off-by-one in interval coalescing changes reported coverage. In `/work/variant-pipeline`, `src/coverage/coalesce.rs` consumes records sorted by `(contig_order, start, end)` and emits canonical half-open genomic intervals. The downstream VCF writer assumes that intervals on each contig are strictly ordered, nonempty, and nonadjacent; the union of emitted intervals equals the union of input intervals; and `depth` is the sum of input depths at every covered base, saturating only when the documented `u64` bound is exceeded. Empty intervals may appear in input and must not create coverage.

The current core is:

```rust
pub fn coalesce(xs: &[Interval]) -> Vec<Interval> {
    let mut out = Vec::new();
    for x in xs {
        if let Some(last) = out.last_mut() {
            if last.contig == x.contig && x.start <= last.end {
                last.end = last.end.max(x.end);
                last.depth = last.depth.saturating_add(x.depth);
                continue;
            }
        }
        out.push(x.clone());
    }
    out
}
```

`Interval { contig: u16, start: u64, end: u64, depth: u64 }` uses `[start,end)`, but the sort comparator and depth semantics are undocumented. Property testing already found:

```text
proptest failure: input chr7:[10,12) depth=5, chr7:[12,15) depth=7
expected components=2, output=[10,15) depth=12
second case: chr7:[10,14) depth=5, chr7:[12,16) depth=7
output=[10,16) depth=12; bases 10–11 and 14–15 are wrong
```

The component count is intentional: adjacent half-open intervals are not connected, while overlap must coalesce. If one output interval cannot represent piecewise depth, redesign the representation and update the writer rather than weakening the VCF contract.

Inspect the repository and produce a proof-oriented repair. Define exact preconditions and postconditions for contig ordering, empty and adjacent intervals, duplicate records, overflow, and the maximum-coordinate boundary. Either prove the existing implementation under a corrected specification or patch it and prove the patch in Lean 4 + Mathlib in `proofs/Coalesce.lean`, with no `sorry` or nonstandard axioms. Add a refinement argument relating the functional model to the Rust loop, executable counterexamples for every rejected assumption, and bounded exhaustive tests for coordinates `0..8`. Update `/work/variant-pipeline/spec/coverage.md` and CI so `cargo test`, Miri, and the Lean proof are required.

