I am coding a custom Android soft keyboard and encountering a bug where, when the keyboard is downsized, the keys shrink as expected but the keyboard does not drop down to the bottom of the screen. Only when certain keys are pressed on the downsized keyboard does it drop to the bottom of the screen.

There is no bug when the keyboard grows in size. In the input method service's `onStartInputView`, I have the following:

```
  @Override
  public void onStartInputView(final EditorInfo editorInfo, final boolean isRestarting)
  {
    super.onStartInputView(editorInfo, isRestarting);

    for (final Keyboard keyboard : keyboardSet)
    {
      keyboard.adjustKeyboardHeight();
    }
    inputContainer.updateHeight();
    // etc.
```

`keyboard.adjustKeyboardHeight()` applies a multiplier to the y-directional variables of each key.
`inputContainer.updateHeight()` calls `requestLayout()`on the View the holds the keyboard and its keys.

How can I fix the bug?

On top of that fix, make the shrink path hold still when a foldable posture change or a second display calls `onStartInputView` while `inputContainer.updateHeight()` is still requesting layout, persist the height multiplier across process death without a visible jump, and add an instrumentation check that fails if any key's window Y trails the container after a downsize.

